10	162	206	126	\N	Standard chunk	\N	GTE Series Gateway Field Installation and Maintenance Guide\n\nDocument Number: GL-OPS-2024-009\n\nVersion: V2.6\n\nModels covered: GTE-3000, GTE-3000S, and GTE-3000Pro\n\nPrepared by: Technical Service Department\n\n1. Preparation Before Operation\n\nBefore on-site operation, three confirmations must be completed: first, confirm that the ambient temperature at the installation location does not exceed 60°C long-term, and is away from strong interference sources such as inverters and large power contactors; second, confirm that the on-site power supply is DC 9V to 36V, and an independent circuit breaker is reserved; third, confirm the network conditions, wired access requires pre-laid network cables, and 4G/5G access requires confirmation that the signal strength on-site is no less than -95dBm.\n\nList of Tools:\n\n2. Installation steps\n\n1. Disconnect the on-site power supply, confirm the power indicator light is off before proceeding with wiring work.\n\n2. Insert the gateway's snap hook into the DIN rail, first hang the side then push down to secure, you can hear the snap hook in place sound; for wall mounting, use M4 screws to fix the four corners.\n\n3. Connect power supply: the 3-pin terminal from left to right is V+, V-, PE, PE must be connected to the grounding busbar of the cabinet, grounding resistance should not exceed 4Ω.\n\n4. Connecting to RS485: A connects to A, B connects to B, 120Ω terminal resistor is enabled at both ends of the bus, and the shield is grounded at one end	[-0.032418057,0.01967433,-0.015544727,0.026964176,-0.018989872,0.002467773,-0.0255046,0.0035287733,0.04285403,0.052413095,0.00075657724,0.017461523,0.004421547,-0.018031089,-0.027362343,0.0064501865,-0.02814442,-0.0069772224,-0.042626027,0.008269158,0.002401276,-0.007853002,-0.020006305,-0.029082514,-0.007080724,0.03663604,-0.018653471,-0.0064500053,0.06546016,0.024064232,-0.0149608385,0.011877198,-0.02528256,-0.029809987,-0.0032491793,-0.042514