91	207	207	131	203	Child chunk	\N	4 days; for those with a tenure of five years, an additional 6 days. Welfare annual leave is combined with statutory annual leave and used together, valid for the current year, not carried over to the next year, and not converted into salary.\n\nAn employee who has worked for at least 1 year in the company is entitled to an additional 2 days of benefits leave; 3 years, 4 days; and 5 years, 6 days. Benefits leave and statutory leave are combined for use, and it is valid for the current year, not carried over to the next year, and not converted into salary.\n\nArticle 10: Sick Leave:\nSick leave must be supported by a sick leave note and registration records from a hospital of level two or higher. If the total sick leave in a year does not exceed 10 days, it will be paid at 80% of the basic salary; for days exceeding 10, it will be paid at 80% of the local minimum wage standard.\nIf the sick leave exceeds 15 days consecutively, the employee must submit a return-to-work certificate before resuming work.\n\nThe medical leave is determined based on the length of service according to national regulations, and the company will not terminate the employment contract during the medical leave period.\n\nArticle 11: Personal Leave:\nPersonal leave is unpaid leave, and the salary will be deducted according to the daily wage standard. Daily wage = monthly wage ÷ 21.75.\nAnnual leave for personal reasons	[0.0019796384,-0.011158484,-0.0034737813,0.039442193,0.021507515,0.017039228,0.02702503,-0.037238088,-0.016019957,0.057776902,0.030691115,0.030574448,0.03472294,-0.007747608,-0.01351351,0.009560641,-0.052751817,-0.046188507,-0.041307617,0.048792478,0.00524937,0.0054211044,-0.043352507,-0.00011237795,-0.013178542,0.020364556,-0.0095546385,-0.0043453476,0.061995983,0.034686726,-0.036671184,-0.016306957,-0.0018542248,-0.062531725,-0.013993807,-0.011294985,0.024981244,-0.07354667,0.0033892477,-0.010911685,0.010914922,-0.010909007,0.014399734,-0.013263