12	164	206	126	\N	Standard chunk	\N	.\n\nAnnual maintenance: Check if the power adapter output voltage has decayed, evaluate if the firmware version needs to be upgraded, perform a master-slave switch exercise for dual-machine hot standby devices.\n\n5. Common on-site fault handling\n\nPWR light not lit: First measure the input voltage at the terminal, check the upstream circuit breaker and wiring if no voltage, if voltage exists but the device does not light up, replace the power adapter.\n\nSYS light flashing rapidly: System anomaly, first power off and reboot; if still flashing rapidly after reboot, export logs and contact technical service department.\n\nCOM light not flashing: No data transmission on the serial port, troubleshoot in the order of A/B wiring reversed, parameter inconsistency, slave station address error, missing terminal resistor.\n\nCollection group reports ERR-5021: Position configuration is incompatible with the protocol stack, commonly occurs after firmware upgrade across major versions, rollback firmware and reupgrade according to the transitional version.\n\nDevice frequently reboots: Troubleshoot in the order of stable power supply, environmental temperature exceeding 60°C, number of edge models exceeding 3.\n\n6. Safety precautions\n\nDo not connect wires while powered on; must work after disconnecting and testing for electricity.\n\nWear anti-static wristband before disassembling the motherboard, hold the motherboard edges, do not touch chip pins.\n\nUse safety harness for high-altitude work, use insulating ladder for cabinet top installation.\n\nAfter completing the job, count the tools to prevent metal tools from being left in the cabinet, causing short circuits	[-0.039239466,-0.024274664,-0.012274367,0.04441835,-0.016775165,-0.02404717,0.010234945,-0.005260749,0.058908224,0.055624556,0.011140647,-0.002765392,0.0059235557,-0.028752698,-0.030448848,0.0035860147,0.014945775,-0.010200474,-0.042057954,-0.023863874,0.029172907,-0.053376496,