23	175	206	128	\N	Standard chunk	\N	2. Fixed the data order disorder issue during disconnection recovery, with the recovery queue now strictly sorted by timestamp\n3. Fixed the issue where DO output status was not reset after importing a configuration file\n4. Fixed the issue where OPC UA Server did not release sessions after abnormal client disconnection, rejecting new connections after exceeding 64 sessions\n5. Fixed the issue where log timestamps were set to 1970 when the device time was not synchronized\n\nKnown Issues:\n1. GTE-3000Pro has high memory usage when running more than four ONNX models simultaneously, suggesting no more than three models per device\n2. FOCAS protocol connection to some older FANUC systems is slow on the first handshake, taking about 20 seconds\n\nIV. Pre-upgrade Preparation\n\n1. Export the current configuration from the Web interface under [System Maintenance] → [Configuration Management], with the filename recommended to include a date, for example line3-gw01-20241220.glcfg\n2. Export the last 7 days' logs from [System Maintenance] → [Log Download], for comparison after upgrade\n3. Ensure the device power supply is stable, as power interruption during upgrade may damage the firmware, requiring factory re-flashing\n4. Verify that the current firmware version matches the target firmware version's major version number\n5. Notify relevant production line personnel that data collection will be interrupted for 3 to 5 minutes during the upgrade\n\nFive, Upgrade Operation Steps\n\nMethod One: Web Interface Upgrade (Recommended)\n\n1. | Access device management via browser |	[0.0016458689,-0.0017454278,-0.02199287,0.046644107,-0.015588211,-0.024665218,-0.0045395857,-0.03413913,0.08212453,0.056423258,0.019299908,0.027606623,0.02409332,-0.012872554,-0.039281372,0.010309351,-0.005871436,-0.02030375,-0.029888052,-0.008791946,0.023906995,-0.045108438,-0.027831815,-0.07259198,-0.027966293,0.026626991,-0.036555167,0.0057491236,0.059249405,0.0391092