25	177	206	128	\N	Standard chunk	\N	. The platform pushes firmware in groups, supporting batch gray release: first upgrade 10% of devices, observe 24 hours without anomalies, then push the remaining devices.\n\nSix, Handling Upgrade Failures\n\nPhenomenon One: After uploading the firmware package, it prompts "Signature Verification Failed"\nThe cause is that the firmware package is incomplete or from an untrusted source. Redownload from the official channel and verify the SHA256 checksum\n\nPhenomenon Two: Prompt "Model Mismatch"\nThe firmware package for GTE-3000 and GTE-3000S is not interchangeable. Check the model identifier in the package name\n\nPhenomenon Three: The device is inaccessible after the upgrade\nFirst confirm whether the management port IP has changed. Access 192.168.1.10 directly. If still inaccessible, hold RESET for 10 seconds to restore factory settings, then import the configuration file exported before the upgrade\n\nPhenomenon Four: The collection groups do not run after the upgrade, and the log shows ERR-5021\nThis is due to incompatibility between the point configuration and the new version protocol stack, commonly seen when upgrading from 2.x to 3.x. Roll back to the version before the upgrade, and reupgrade through the 2.9.20 transitional version\n\nSeven, Firmware Rollback\n\nDevices retain the firmware image of the previous version. Click "Rollback to Previous Version" on the [System Maintenance] → [Firmware Upgrade] page. The rollback process takes approximately 2 minutes. Only one historical version is retained. After two consecutive upgrades, rollback to an earlier version is not possible.	[-0.009122455,0.0011623226,-0.024591535,0.05649124,-0.022064075,0.00651044,0.0047969427,-0.014394173,0.042676777,0.07069679,0.01900921,0.009632451,0.022653705,-0.045606,-0.037307277,0.029519916,-0.0041890233,-0.005928401,-0.013172533,0.0072003785,0.052414525,-0.035801027,-0.018022968,-0.04512482,0.015965497,0.041391596,-0.036796067,0.0047980146,0.