22	174	206	128	\N	Standard chunk	\N	.\n\nII. Current Maintenance Versions\n\n3.2.14-r5   Stable version, released in September 2024, recommended for production environments\n3.3.6-r2    Feature version, released in December 2024, supports 5G dual SIM dual standby and MQTT 5.0\n2.9.20-r8   Maintenance version, only fixes critical defects, maintenance stops on December 31, 2025\n\nIII. Major Changes in 3.3.6\n\nNew Features:\n1. MQTT 5.0 support, supports shared subscriptions and topic aliases, reducing message overhead by about 15% in long connection scenarios\n2. GTE-3000S and GTE-3000Pro support 5G dual SIM dual standby, automatically switching to the backup SIM within 30 seconds when the main SIM fails\n3. Collection groups support importing and exporting to Excel, including fields such as point name, register address, data type, and scaling coefficient\n4. Web interface adds a "Communication Quality" panel, displaying response time and timeout rate for each southbound device\n5. Edge rules support window functions, allowing calculation of 5-minute sliding averages\n\nBug Fixes:\n1. Fixed the occasional frame loss issue with RS485 at 115200bps over long periods, caused by the serial port driver buffer not being cleared in high load conditions\n2. Fixed the data order disorder issue during disconnection recovery, with the recovery queue now strictly sorted by timestamp\n3. | Configuration file import fixes DO |	[-0.007429306,-0.025273196,-0.023012972,0.069640145,0.005935689,0.011899067,-0.0016054747,-0.04761853,0.056478046,0.04072326,-0.029446386,0.029705862,0.008739165,-0.021559503,-0.035173584,-0.016668709,-0.03247924,-0.026928483,-0.010033582,0.005671249,0.03953051,-0.008952877,-0.033977162,-0.044761084,-0.022426315,0.06448074,-0.05525311,0.036782615,0.0544371,0.031825133,-0.0066363807,-0.025446622,-0.013515877,-0.015859174,-0.010468036,-0.036108125,-0.019776935,0.02366829,-0.043050382,-0.024975952,0.022463005,-0.016160049,0.025325036,-0.02540772,-0.035919316,-0