79	192	207	129	191	Child chunk	\N	Or cumulative absence from work for 5 days, fighting or brawling at the workplace, or serious negligence causing significant economic loss. In such cases, the company may terminate the employment contract immediately.\n\n## Chapter Eight Employee Departure Management\n\nArticle 31 Employees must complete work handover, including pending matters, documents, office equipment, access cards, and account permissions. After the handover is completed and both parties sign to confirm, the Human Resources Department will process the departure procedures.\n\nArticle 32 The company shall issue a departure certificate upon termination or termination of the labor contract and shall complete the transfer of employee records and benefits records within 15 days.\n\nArticle 33 The salary for the month of departure shall be paid together with the regular salary on the next normal payroll date. Unused statutory annual leave shall be paid at 300% of the daily wage.\n\n## Chapter Nine Supplementary Provisions\n\nArticle 34: This manual is interpreted and revised by the Human Resources Department. The revised version shall be approved by the General Manager	[-0.019143594,-0.026713349,-0.024763953,0.03417706,0.023592804,-0.010802615,-0.0047137015,-0.04249768,-0.0026568177,0.06897182,0.03625669,0.041197326,-0.027968638,-0.021804795,-0.026802097,-0.012699494,-0.03593163,-0.017964529,-0.042975258,0.023269057,0.0039391397,-0.02684228,-0.029390741,-0.04501947,0.017807042,0.03703459,0.022240546,-0.03471709,0.047194395,0.030958563,-0.05334948,-0.021033656,0.009634725,-0.0631127,-0.012633014,-0.018188512,0.035477042,-0.042996153,-0.004186349,0.002353914,-0.017107438,-0.010078347,0.050300494,-0.033314675,-0.008011658,-0.038373835,-0.025968874,0.019401059,0.014730219,-0.033274543,0.03390546,0.0069082133,0.025469849,-0.024143606,0.047083072,-0.012912335,-0.027883437,-0.0019809352,-0.030029798,0.08166115,0.011243115,-0.018167794,0.014016534,-0.037687905,0.00376383,0.