30	198	207	130	194	Child chunk	\N	, 25th of each month. Expense reports completed by the finance department within 3 working days before the payment date are included in the current payment period; otherwise, they are postponed to the next period.\n\nArticle 12: Loan Management: Single prepayment loans shall not exceed 80% of the estimated expenses. The loan must be settled within 10 working days after the business trip. No new loan can be issued if the previous loan has not been settled.\n\nChapter Four: Violation Handling\n\nArticle 13: Full reimbursement will be reclaimed for fake invoices, false expense reporting, and splitting invoices to bypass approval. Such actions will be treated as serious violations according to Article 30 of the employee handbook.\n\nArticle 14 The Treasury conducts quarterly spot checks of reimbursement documents, which are not less than 10 per cent and the results are reported to the General Manager.\n\nChapter Five: Supplementary Provisions\n\nArticle 15: This regulation is interpreted by the Finance Department and will be implemented from the effective date.\n\n| Role | Air travel | Rail travel | Local transportation |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---	[-0.016270014,-0.018670185,0.0045957826,0.030000111,-0.023594704,0.006200975,0.017263243,-0.049954556,0.011876281,0.06756305,0.043330114,0.016106853,0.023049146,-0.0075418022,-0.016623445,0.03164782,-0.048895214,-0.022191228,-0.029801523,0.018068021,-0.0244328,0.0007144671,-0.024955781,-0.0064973626,-0.035714775,0.04115845,0.0152212465,0.0017652125,0.090891354,0.0059696753,-0.019345071,-0.0025106275,0.007033692,0.00027884627,0.011229158,-0.03234702,0.032049723,-0.03458506,0.025742304,-0.03354195,0.046666544,0.019059727,0.017930182,-0.04665955,-0.053448815,-0.052779134,-0.020629931,-0.02688063,0.01666543,-0.03511856,0.016899671,0.013805871,-0.016763283,-0.070684314,0.011418915,-0.0021775612,-0.024049606,-0.06460646,-0.009326712,0.047129977,0.013373337,-0.004546186,0.031801637,-0.03633832,0.02032