93	210	207	131	209	Child chunk	\N	To be used within 12 months, otherwise it will expire.\n\nAn employee who is legally married is entitled to 13 days of marriage leave (including 3 days as stipulated by the state and 10 days as a local reward), including weekends and public holidays. The marriage leave must be taken within 12 months from the date of marriage registration, and it will expire if not taken within that period.\n\nArticle 13: Maternity Leave and Paternity Leave:\nFemale employees are entitled to 158 days of maternity leave, with 15 days available before childbirth. An additional 15 days will be granted for difficult childbirth, and an additional 15 days for each additional child.\nMale employees are entitled to 15 days of paternity leave, which must be taken within 3 months from the date of their spouse's childbirth.\n\nFemale employees are entitled to 1 hour of breastfeeding time per day for the first year of their child's life, which can be combined as an hour earlier departure each day.\n\nArticle 14: Childcare Leave:\n\nBoth parents are entitled to 10 days of childcare leave per year before their child turns 3 years old. Childcare leave is paid based on attendance, and it is not carried over if not taken in the same year.\n\nFor the death of direct relatives (parents, spouse, children), 3 days of bereavement leave is granted; for the death of grandparents, maternal grandparents, and parents-in-law, 1 day of bereavement leave is granted. If the employee needs to travel out of town for the funeral, additional travel leave will be given based on the ticket, up to a maximum of 2 days.	[0.00087944564,0.01891857,-0.010639195,-0.008743145,-0.009514568,0.012031292,0.007278757,-0.014140679,0.027046805,0.0296577,0.047802616,0.015388114,0.027139446,-0.0058721476,-0.007832444,0.032302238,-0.04457734,-0.027671892,-0.030542348,0.030141387,-0.042762987,0.040964045,-0.023139624,-0.013939478,-0.008956309,0.05279436,0.0024915494,-0.001192767,0.054810055,0.0055000056,-