96	213	207	131	209	Child chunk	\N	Overtime Application.\n\nArticle 22 - Overtime compensation methods:\n\nOvertime on workdays       Converted to compensatory leave at 1.5 times, or paid at 1.5 times the regular rate\nOvertime on rest days           Prioritizing compensatory leave of the same duration, or paid at 2 times the regular rate if compensatory leave is not possible\nOvertime on statutory holidays       Paid at 3 times the regular rate, and compensatory leave cannot be used as a substitute\n\nArticle 23 - Compensatory leave must be used within 3 months from the date of overtime, or it will expire. The minimum unit of compensatory leave is 0.5 days.\n\nArticle 24 - For positions under the comprehensive working hour system, overtime is calculated based on the total working hours exceeding the statutory standard within the monthly cycle, not on a daily basis.\n\nChapter Five - Attendance Statistics and Appeals\n\nArticle 25 - The Human Resources Department generates the attendance report for the previous month by the 3rd of each month and sends it to the department heads for confirmation.\n\nArticle 26: Employees have the right to review attendance records,	[0.0025203105,0.00462886,-0.0064203166,0.039031222,-0.009554506,0.03337315,-0.0061795376,-0.032105822,-0.0018773965,0.052207578,0.0091816075,0.03844682,0.006883949,-0.022578565,0.011163685,0.010848671,-0.050063767,-0.033498276,-0.031906303,0.027673075,-0.0053770393,0.018902482,-0.021181324,-0.04122617,0.00052702817,0.023010172,0.029708048,-0.006486614,0.051217083,0.024830984,-0.07095676,-0.021206392,0.006069015,-0.058511883,0.032978952,-0.010392643,0.03893029,-0.039892953,0.003741793,-0.0058916532,-0.0032197472,-0.00049082865,-0.0006361801,-0.0124507,-0.025654385,-0.055800047,-0.042933073,0.020558078,0.03109842,0.009024508,0.007355239,0.018999167,0.0024890064,-0.023585977,0.0682465,0.018887343,-0.014798652,-0.0410683,-0.003607242,0.039004903,-0.010962951,0.008665362,-0.0041954876,-0.03442835,0.023560287,0.0