166	456	208	134	\N	Standard chunk	\N	If the status is "Connected", it indicates that the network and authentication are normal, and the issue is likely in topic mapping or platform-side subscription; if the status is "Reconnecting", it indicates network or certificate issues. Check if the device can ping the platform domain name, whether the certificate has expired, and whether the system time is accurate. System time deviation exceeding 5 minutes can cause TLS handshake failure\n\n## IV. Faults and Alarms\n\n### Q14: What does the error code ERR-5021 mean?\n\nERR-5021 indicates incompatibility between point configuration and the protocol stack, commonly occurring after cross-major version firmware upgrades. The solution is to roll back to the firmware version before the upgrade, and follow the instructions in the [Firmware Upgrade and Version Release Notes] to first upgrade to the transitional version before the target version.\n\n### Q15: Why does the device frequently restart?\n\nThe three most common reasons are:\n\n1. Yes. Download the Excel template from [Device Management] → [Point Management], fill in the point name, register address, data type, scaling coefficient, unit, and other fields according to the template, and import it. Single import is limited to no more than 5000 rows, and batch imports are required if exceeded	[-0.030333577,0.00462364,-0.007962135,0.050511535,-0.009094366,-0.0074462793,0.045380533,-0.030759076,0.049256865,0.056711987,0.0072206473,0.0141834915,0.012768528,-0.021846911,-0.024910728,0.011857432,-0.017927159,-0.006964365,-0.009017502,-0.0011364878,0.037156817,-0.0033070422,-0.029637398,-0.03207151,-0.009557042,0.072351135,-0.023981635,0.04276565,0.078135826,0.0886723,-0.01753358,-0.004671344,-0.016474089,-0.024223328,-0.0013802531,-0.019939277,-0.019746715,-0.0077546644,-0.02465933,-0.06537835,-0.010434318,0.0028201586,0.0153437825,-0.04886126,-0.019159703,-0.0017972859,-0.03253197,-0.0029530704,-0.013206932,-0.040623784,-0.01973487